# Firecracker / jailer pin.
#
# The audit value of this backend is upstream's, so the binaries are the
# upstream release artifacts, byte for byte — never a local build and
# never "latest". `utils/install-firecracker.sh` reads this file, and
# `k7d doctor` reports the version and the sha it found on the node.
#
# Why v1.16.1: newest stable release when the backend landed, and
# its swagger carries everything the later increments need —
# `network_overrides`, `vsock_override` and `clock_realtime` on
# `PUT /snapshot/load` and `PATCH /drives` slot fill.
# MPTable (legacy, non-ACPI) boot is still supported, which is what
# `guest/kernel/config-minimal` needs.
#
# Bumping: change the version and all three sha256 values together.
# Get them from the release's own SHA256SUMS asset, or:
#   curl -fsSL <FIRECRACKER_RELEASE_URL> | sha256sum
#   tar xzf …tgz && sha256sum release-*/firecracker-* release-*/jailer-*
FIRECRACKER_VERSION=v1.16.1
FIRECRACKER_RELEASE_URL=https://github.com/firecracker-microvm/firecracker/releases/download/v1.16.1/firecracker-v1.16.1-x86_64.tgz
FIRECRACKER_TGZ_SHA256=382a02a869e4d6d5cb14c40577f9545e8458021ea8b0b2d3fc10ec14d9c242e6
FIRECRACKER_SHA256=2fd0171309af7e24cf8dafc8a6f921c1434c49b5f9349bb996b7ed0a4deb8aa7
JAILER_SHA256=1f3a0c1fe86212d0001819bfe0819071c01208b3ccc9398c3b3bc1b84cf21edd
